  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"fdasrsf\" %}\n{% set version = \"2.6.10\" %}\n\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/{{ name[0] }}/{{ name }}/fdasrsf-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 0108d01ca3aeace0abd1131f4928f16aa833e88dfb93b6b4e4f87d0b7c018102\n\nbuild:\n  skip: true  # [py<310]\n  number: 2\n  # --no-build-isolation is the key change: without it pip ignores the host\n  # env and downloads setuptools/wheel/cffi/Cython/findblas/numpy from PyPI,\n  # so the extensions get compiled against whatever numpy PyPI happens to\n  # offer for that interpreter (2.2.6 on py310, 2.4.6 on py311, 2.5.2 on\n  # py312+) rather than against the conda-forge numpy in host.\n  script: {{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python                               # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}   # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - numpy                                # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cython                               # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cffi >=1.0.0                         # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - findblas                             # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ compiler('c') }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    # upstream pyproject caps this: requires = [\"setuptools<=73.0.1\", ...].\n    # With build isolation removed, the cap has to be honoured here instead.\n    - setuptools <=73.0.1\n    - wheel\n    - numpy\n    - cffi >=1.0.0\n    - findblas\n    - cython >=0.29.17\n    # findblas links the extensions against BLAS at build time\n    - libblas\n    - libcblas\n    - liblapack\n    - blas-devel\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy >=1.25\n    - cffi >=1.0.0\n    - cython >=0.29.17\n    - joblib >=0.16.0\n    - matplotlib-base\n    - numba >=0.51.2\n    - patsy\n    - pyparsing\n    - scipy >=1.14\n    - six\n    - tqdm\n\ntest:\n  imports:\n    - fdasrsf\n    # exercise the compiled extensions, not just the pure-python package\n    - optimum_reparamN2\n    - cbayesian\n    - crbfgs\n    - cimage\n  commands:\n    - pip check\n  requires:\n    - pip\n\nabout:\n  home: http://research.tetonedge.net\n  summary: functional data analysis using the square root slope framework\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n  description: |\n    A python package for functional data analysis using the square root\n    slope framework and curves using the square root velocity framework\n    which performs pair-wise and group-wise alignment as well as modeling\n    using functional component analysis and regression.\n  doc_url: https://fdasrsf-python.readthedocs.io/\n  dev_url: https://github.com/jdtuck/fdasrsf_python\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jdtuck\n",
